$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A mixture of 2-substituted pyrazine S1 (2.0
mmol), benzyl bromide or isopropyl 2-(bromomethyl)benzoate (3.0 mmol)
were dissolved in acetone (3.0 mL). The resulted mixture was refluxed
overnight. The resulting precipitate was collected and rinsed with cold
acetone and ethyl acetate. To further purify the salt, it could be
recrystallized from dichloromethane and ethyl acetate. If the desired
pyrazinium salt didn’t precipitate, the reaction mixture was concentrated
in vacuoand the crude salt was purified by column chromatography on
silica gel using dichloromethane/methanol (20:1) as the eluent.
2-Methyl-6-(4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl)pyrazine (S3j): 886 mg, white
solid. mp 59- 60 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.86 (s, 1H), 8.46 (s,
1H), 8.14 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 2H), 7.76 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 2H), 2.65 (s, 3H);
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 153.6, 150.1, 143.6, 140.0, 139.1, 131.5 (q,
JC-F = 32.4 Hz), 127.3, 125.9 (q, JC-F = 3.8 Hz), 124.0 (q, JC-F = 270.6
Hz), 21.7. 19F NMR (376 MHz, CDCl3) δ -62.7. HRMS Calculated for
C12H10F3N2[M+H]+ 239.0791, found 239.0791.
