$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 8-(3-Chloro-5-(4-(piperidin-1-yl)phenyl)pyridin-4-yl)-2,8-diazaspiro[4.5]decan-1-one
(65) 8-(3-Bromo-5-chloropyridin-4-yl)-2,8-diazaspiro[4.5]decan-1-one 57
(35 mg, 0.10 mmol), 1-(4-
(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)phenyl)piperidine (32 mg,
0.11 mmol) and Pd(dppf)Cl2.CH2Cl2 (3.7 mg, 5.1 μmol) were loaded in a
microwave vial under argon and then degassed. MeCN (1.8 mL) and 0.5 M
aqueous sodium carbonate solution (284 μL, 0.142 mmol) were added. The
reaction mixture was heated under microwave irradiation at 120 °C for 60
min. The solvent was evaporated and the crude material was dry loaded and
purified via Biotage column chromatography (CH2Cl2/EtOH, 98/2 to 95/5).
The title compound 65 (40 mg, 93% yield) as a cream solid. 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.30-1.36 (m, 2H), 1.58-1.64 (m, 2H), 1.70-1.77 (m, 4H),
1.94-2.02 (m, 4H), 2.68-2.76 (m, 2H), 3.09-3.15 (m, 2H), 3.21-3.25 (m,
4H), 3.29 (t, J = 6.9 Hz, 2H), 6.17 (bs, 1H), 6.97-7.01 (m, 2H),
7.13-7.17 (m, 2H), 8.18 (s, 1H), 8.38 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ
24.4, 25.9, 31.5, 32.4, 38.8, 42.0, 47.7, 50.3, 116.0, 127.9, 128.4,
130.0, 134.1, 149.0, 151.1, 151.6, 152.9, 181.8; LC (Method C) - MS (ESI,
m/z) Rt = 1.96 min – 425/427 (M+H)+. ESI-HRMS: Found: 425.2100 calculated
for C24H30 35ClN4O (M+H)+: 425.2103.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, microwave irradiation, thermal, microwave vial used,
Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Potent, Orally Bioavailable, Small-Molecule Inhibitors of
WNT Signaling from a Cell-Based Pathway Screen
